  "generated_answer": "## Class 5 Science Coverage\n\nBased on the retrieved curriculum evidence, Class 5 (Primary 5) Science is organised into the following units:\n\n- **Sources, uses of and properties of water** (C5-U01)\n- **Water purification** (C5-U02)\n- **Water Cycle** (C5-U03)\n- **Simple machines** (C5-U04)\n- **Soil Components, Types and Uses** (C5-U05)\n- **Soil Conservation** (C5-U06)\n- **Forest Reserves** (C5-U07)\n- **Chemical Processes in the Home** (C5-U08)\n- **Disease Prevention** (C5-U09)\n- **Puberty and changes** (C5-U10)\n\n### Learning Outcomes (example from Chemical Processes in the Home)\nFor the unit **Chemical Processes in the Home** (C5-U08), the following learning outcomes are specified:\n\n- **C5U08-LO01** \u2014 Explain what a chemical reaction is.\n- **C5U08-LO02** \u2014 State some chemical processes in the home.\n- **C5U08-LO03** \u2014 Explain how foofoo is made.\n- **C5U08-LO04** \u2014 Explain how ogiri is made.\n- **C5U08-LO05** \u2014 Explain how local soap is made. Discuss about preservation of foofoo, ogiri and local soap.\n\nNote: Learning outcomes for the other units (C5-U01 to C5-U07, C5-U09, C5-U10) were not provided in the retrieved evidence.",
